{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta","id":1529718,"title":"The Fluffy Puppy Thread - Post your favorite NPCs, characters, and things about W:TA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-30T08:11:11-08:00","id":1529718,"title":"The Fluffy Puppy Thread - Post your favorite NPCs, characters, and things about W:TA","content":"Exactly what the thread title says.<br /> <br /> What is your favorite thing, be it adventure, character, subsidiary, or tribe from W:TA.<br /> <br /> Only positive things.<br /> <br /> Let the Gnosis flow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T09:48:18-08:00","id":1529722,"title":"","content":"Well it seems only right to start with WEREWOLF: THE WILD WEST (The sourcebook) and THE WYLD WEST as a setting, since this was the hook that really pulled me into the World of Darkness (VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE - REDEMPTION made the original introduction, but I\u2019ve always leaned much more to Van Helsing than Count Dracula).<br /> <br /> Also, there\u2019s something inherently gleeful in the High Concept of \u2018Werewolf Cowboys Vs Manifest Destiny\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of favourite characters, just about every signature character commands a share of my affections (Yes, that includes Evan Heals-the-Past, I am a soft-hearted fan) but Vic Stryker, with or without the Eagle\u2019s Nest Pack, is a special favourite: he\u2019s the perfect mixture of Pulp Werewolf Fantasy with pure pathos and personal tragedy.<br /> <br /> I like to think that he and King Jonas Albrecht (Another favourite) made at least one joke about finally having the perfect pair of eyes if they ever met (and it\u2019s easy to imagine a hard-charging King with a spymaster grandfather and trouble with in-house personnel having <i>plenty</i> of uses for a trustworthy PI).<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of Garou Tribes I have to say \u201cAll of them\u201d but one must admit to loving some more than others: reading through the BY NIGHT version of WtA led me to an interesting revelation - almost all of my particular favourites were with the Sanctum of Gaia (Black Furies, Fianna, Silver Fangs, W******), though one must admit to having a real soft spot for the Bone Gnawers and U***** over on the other side.<br /> <br /> Oh, and mustn\u2019t miss the Silent Striders, steering a risky course somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for favourite Pentex subsidiary, it\u2019s definitely the Black Dog gaming factory: ask me about my takes on their various game lines (How they differ from and resemble the \u2018real\u2019 World of Darkness) only if you have free time and patience with rambling enthusiasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T10:49:21-08:00","id":1529723,"title":"","content":"The redemption of Bat has always been my favourite plot event. It is so rare to see actual progress made in the game, plus it showcases where the Shadow Lords differ from the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords work to make up for their mistakes. The tribe killed the Camazotz, and centuries later a pack of Lords with heritage to those who did the deed go on an epic umbral quest and redeem a part of Bat back to Gaia.<br /> <br /> It is also one of my favourite crossover events, as Lords and Tzimisce have been enemies for easily millennia if not more. And Tzimisce have their giant bat monster form. AND Europe has no vampire bats. It doesn't justify how the Lords reacted but it gives a very good reason WHY.<br /> <br /> The second crossover I love is the Silent Strider curse. They lost Egypt and if they stay long in one place ghosts are attracted to them. Hence they travel all around. Everything is set up so it is not a chore to play but ADDS to the play and in a lot of ways demystifies the tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T12:49:03-08:00","id":1529731,"title":"","content":"For me it's a three way tie between Iona Kinslayer, Gretchen Valkenburg, and Sept of the Fanum. I often name-drop them if not find a way to work them directly into stories. The Fanum is a great resource for Garou research and being a source of lore, presented in a more straightforward manner. Gretchen is great for bankrolling humanitarian efforts (particularly wolf conservation) without having to default to the Glass Walkers, and Iona is just straight up badass in every sense of the word. Love her story, love the freebooters, and love her silver sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T01:38:21-08:00","id":1529744,"title":"","content":"Favourites, ok.<br /> <br /> Tribe- Black Furies ( w Older Brother and Red Talons close behind)<br /> Auspice- Theurge.<br /> Breed- This ones a three way tie.<br /> Caern/Sept- Namorrkan<br /> Fera- Gumargan/Rokea.<br /> Canon NPC- Kisasi<br /> P/Matron- Seiryuu/Crocodile.<br /> Adventure- The Broken Brother<br /> Subsidiary- Hallahan.....a lot of my Chronicles are coastal or archipelago based.<br /> Gift- Crocodile Pact or Paws of the New Born Cub.<br /> Rite- Spirit Awakening/Prayer for the Prey<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T04:39:19-08:00","id":1529748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The redemption of Bat has always been my favourite plot event. It is so rare to see actual progress made in the game, plus it showcases where the Shadow Lords differ from the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords work to make up for their mistakes. The tribe killed the Camazotz, and centuries later a pack of Lords with heritage to those who did the deed go on an epic umbral quest and redeem a part of Bat back to Gaia </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> On the one hand this is an excellent pick and a sound point; on the other hand I didn\u2019t make the name of a Savage West Silver Fang my username to take this sort of thing lying belly-up; however one doesn\u2019t want to start a correspondence off on the wrong footing.<br /> <br /> Therefore to heck with serious analysis, time to give that imp of mischief on my shoulder a hearing - it\u2019s a good thing Shadow Lords had at least one major offence to make amends for, because atoning for all their lesser offences would have taken the whole tribe and the whole tribe would have died of exhaustion halfway through the old rap-sheet.\ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m also tempted to make a joke about Silver Fangs clearly making fair payment for all their Sins by suffering through the ongoing purgatory of trying to lead the Garou Nation as anything like a United Front \u2026 and I\u2019ve never been good at resisting temptation, as you see).<br /> <br /> <br /> In all seriousness it\u2019s always delightful to see the Shadow Lords as villainous in style, rather than in substance (and the Lords do so love their diabolical flourishes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T22:03:49-08:00","id":1529884,"title":"","content":"The Rokea and Mokole absolutely cemented by interest in W:tA back in the day, particularly because they had a promise of a structure mythos to them. And they remain my favorite parts of the setting, especially when hammering home just how different this game is from Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T06:38:11-08:00","id":1529898,"title":"","content":"To me, the two biggest draws of Werewolf are Family and Culture. Fundamentally it's a game about communities that share history, laws, culture and family.<br /> <br /> Family is crucial to Werewolf - in the sense of blood relations, in the sense of found family and ultimatley in the sense of belonging to the World and being responsible to it.<br /> <br /> Ancestors, kinfolk, traditions, local folkore and landmarks and ultimatley lived legends all make up who you are and where you came from. You belong somewhere and you have a duty to protect it. You fight for you own and what the people that came before you have fought.<br /> <br /> The pack is the ultimate found family - to the point that they are a close bound intimate union. One where there may be conflict but ultimatley you live and feel their lives with them and your totem. It makes you more whole then you could ever be and allows you to brave the fires of hell.<br /> <br /> This unity is also representd through the Tribes and the Nation. They all have clear history and identity that is defined by a marriage between the culture of the Garou and the people that they live and sleep with. Afterall 9 out of 10 werewolf community members are kin. The views, experiences,languages and cultures of the kin reshape the Garou into their own variant of the Tribe that is still united in praxis, faith and methodology.<br /> <br /> This allows us to bring in the wealth of human experience,myth and faith into the game. This ultimatley reflects the duty of the Garou that is to all of the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T21:09:30-08:00","id":1529959,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say what I love about W:TA the most. It's my second favorite gameline in the setting and always been neck and neck with Mage but as I grow older, I grow less and less enchanted with the kind of apologia that M:TA had toward the Technocracy and more interested in the larger environmental themes of W:TA. I also feel like a lot of what I initially thought was silly in W:TA had been proven to be sadly all too accurate.<br /> <br /> Basically, Pentex is the most realistic and chilling satire in the setting as the real life evil doers aren't tortured antiheroes or ignorant but deliberately horrifically malicious toward the world as well as its people--often for religious accelerationist reasons mixed with their greed. In 2001, I never would have believed a man would burn a forest if he could make as much money growing one. In 2024, I know they'd go out of their way to spend money to burn the forest down.<br /> <br /> I found the<i> Subsidiaries</i> most useful as a sourcebook but my favorite work probably was <i>Rage across Russia</i>.<br /> <br /> Part of what I love is the sense of doomed heroism that comes from the Garou. I love the characters of the game and wish we'd see more novels about them as well as comics. Sadly, they seem to have been left behind for 5th Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T04:27:06-08:00","id":1530017,"title":"","content":"(Ladies, Gentlemen, significant others - I have a confession to make, but please don\u2019t break out the torches and pitchforks: in my own opinion all tie-in novels for RPG settings should be written on the understanding that these are, more or less, the After Action Reports of your own campaign and are therefore completely non-binding on other authors).<br /> <br /> At least I feel this should be the case when dealing with a single-world setting and still more when writing the signature characters of that setting: if nothing else this allows a lot more freedom to interpret and reinterpret those characters, rather than insisting there must be One True Vision.<br /> <br /> Clearly my Silver Fang eccentricity is \u2018Thinks he\u2019s Clever\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T04:34:38-08:00","id":1530018,"title":"","content":"On a slightly less high-handed note, there does seem to be two Signature Characters who made the transition from the classic editions to 5th edition: Mari Cabrah, who is mentioned by name, and King Jonas Albrecht (Whose family is alluded to and whose presence may be inferred through allusions in the Silver Crown\u2019s wrote-up).<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think the most sensible approach is to say that 5th Edition core book is meant to be a start and not the limit of this reimagined setting, so there\u2019s plenty of room for versions of the old Signature Characters - though for my money it makes sense to allow the old Signature Characters to age out of the limelight and give PCs a clearer shot at being The Heroes of this setting.<br /> <br /> If nothing else it\u2019s interesting to wonder what Mari Cabrah would look like somewhere in her early fifties (\u201cFierce\u201d is the word that occurs to me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T05:31:12-08:00","id":1530022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530018#post1530018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On a slightly less high-handed note, there does seem to be two Signature Characters who made the transition from the classic editions to 5th edition: Mari Cabrah, who is mentioned by name, and King Jonas Albrecht (Whose family is alluded to and whose presence may be inferred through allusions in the Silver Crown\u2019s wrote-up).<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think the most sensible approach is to say that 5th Edition core book is meant to be a start and not the limit of this reimagined setting, so there\u2019s plenty of room for versions of the old Signature Characters - though for my money it makes sense to allow the old Signature Characters to age out of the limelight and give PCs a clearer shot at being The Heroes of this setting.<br /> <br /> If nothing else it\u2019s interesting to wonder what Mari Cabrah would look like somewhere in her early fifties (\u201cFierce\u201d is the word that occurs to me).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have every confidence they will eventually reintroduce everything with the big changes effectively written around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T07:43:50-08:00","id":1530026,"title":"","content":"Well hopefully the writers will have the nerve to stick with 5th Edition as a reimagining, rather than a straightforward continuation of the classic editions - if nothing else \u2019Ultimate Werewolf\u2019 is an intriguing premise in the same way \u2018Ultimate Marvel\u2019 was - though I do agree that it would be a very good idea to give that baby an apology for pitching it out with the bathwater, wrap it up warmly then put it to bed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T08:19:34-08:00","id":1530030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530018#post1530018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On a slightly less high-handed note, there does seem to be two Signature Characters who made the transition from the classic editions to 5th edition: Mari Cabrah, who is mentioned by name, and King Jonas Albrecht (Whose family is alluded to and whose presence may be inferred through allusions in the Silver Crown\u2019s wrote-up).<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think the most sensible approach is to say that 5th Edition core book is meant to be a start and not the limit of this reimagined setting, so there\u2019s plenty of room for versions of the old Signature Characters - though for my money it makes sense to allow the old Signature Characters to age out of the limelight and give PCs a clearer shot at being The Heroes of this setting.<br /> <br /> If nothing else it\u2019s interesting to wonder what Mari Cabrah would look like somewhere in her early fifties (\u201cFierce\u201d is the word that occurs to me).</div> </div> </div> </div>While the names appear, they are just a stab at legitimacy and winking at the audience (as said multiple times by the devs). The intention by the authors was to make this an alternate Werewolf without the percieved baggage. Alas, at times they seem to be quite confused on whether they're re-imagining material or just arguing with what they disliked about the older material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T09:21:15-08:00","id":1530037,"title":"","content":"There is a strong sense that 5th edition was put together more via argument than consensus: I\u2019m happy to give the setting further thought, but will likely give the sourcebook itself a mixed-to-negative review.<br /> <br /> It has some good ideas, but leaves them looking very lonely high and dry above a deeply confused, self-critical, even mildly contemptuous look at the Garou Nation and their World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> But enough about the negative, I\u2019d much rather focus on a reimagining than a hatchet job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T10:01:23-08:00","id":1530041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530037#post1530037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is a strong sense that 5th edition was put together more via argument than consensus: I\u2019m happy to give the setting further thought, but will likely give the sourcebook itself a mixed-to-negative review.<br /> <br /> It has some good ideas, but leaves them looking very lonely high and dry above a deeply confused, self-critical, even mildly contemptuous look at the Garou Nation and their World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> But enough about the negative, I\u2019d much rather focus on a reimagining than a hatchet job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have a hard time investing my energy into fixing someone's hatchet job instead of actually playing something that works. I might take a look at W5 in a couple of years when they actually try and engage with the bizarre mirror setting they have born. At this time they're only planning adventures so it's not like we're going to see much development there. Even for Hunter it took quite a while to get something, and it's going to be a book on academics of all things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T10:36:21-08:00","id":1530042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530026#post1530026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well hopefully the writers will have the nerve to stick with 5th Edition as a reimagining, rather than a straightforward continuation of the classic editions - if nothing else \u2019Ultimate Werewolf\u2019 is an intriguing premise in the same way \u2018Ultimate Marvel\u2019 was - though I do agree that it would be a very good idea to give that baby an apology for pitching it out with the bathwater, wrap it up warmly then put it to bed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why in the WORLD would we hope that?<br /> <br /> An Ultimate Werewolf is fine but we had that and still have that. It's called Werewolf: The Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T10:53:17-08:00","id":1530043,"title":"","content":"Really like wild west werewolves because its really cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T15:25:08-08:00","id":1530116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530043#post1530043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really like wild west werewolves because its really cool</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a wolf of most excellent taste!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T21:05:57-08:00","id":1530131,"title":"","content":"I have always enjoyed the character of Vic Stryker. <br /> <br /> I still wish it had been feasible to have a Pulp Era setting book for Werewolf (and Mage and Changeling). <br /> <br /> (I like to imagine that the counterpart to Stryker's Eagle's Nest pack would have been led by a Silver Fang who was allegedly the surviving Tzarina Anastasia and included the period's signature Black Fury, Child of Gaia, Get of Fenris, and Uktena.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T13:54:22-08:00","id":1530201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530131#post1530131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always enjoyed the character of Vic Stryker.<br /> <br /> I still wish it had been feasible to have a Pulp Era setting book for Werewolf (and Mage and Changeling).<br /> <br /> (I like to imagine that the counterpart to Stryker's Eagle's Nest pack would have been led by a Silver Fang who was allegedly the surviving Tzarina Anastasia and included the period's signature Black Fury, Child of Gaia, Get of Fenris, and Uktena.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fellah, I like the cut of your jib: I was actually trying to puzzle out what a pack of friendly rivals to the Eagle\u2019s Nest might look like and had hit on almost exactly the same mix of tribes (Mostly because my working theory - based on WEREWOLF THE WILD WEST - is that the Black Furies, Children of Gaia, Fianna and Uktena, with their absence of background limits at character creation, make the best starting point for a given pack of pregen characters, being infinitely flexible).<br /> <br /> Now since the Eagle\u2019s Nest already has the fiery Lorna McNab, that meant the Fianna would be off the table, so that meant looking elsewhere for the last two members of the team - ticking off the Great Powers of the era already represented by the Eagle\u2019s Nest left me with the USSR, Japan, Germany, Italy and France so I assumed that these friendly rivals would represent the elements in those nations seeking to avoid a Second Great War.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, though, my notion was that the resident Silver Fang might have been one of those claimants to the dignities of House Conquering Claw that pop up from time to time (Without winning much recognition): I have to say that your notion of \u2018Grand Duchess Anastasia\u2019 going through First Change and forming her own pack is far, far more delightfully Pulp.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the record, I\u2019m assuming the pack breakdown is something like:-<br /> <br /> - Ragabash (Uktena, Lupus): Born to one of the last litters of Japanese wolves and adopted by Elder Brother under mysterious circumstances (It\u2019s possible they were originally Hakken but shifted tribes for reasons they do not care to share).<br /> <br /> Owes somebody a favour and is therefore acting as minder to this pack of reckless idealists: also keeps running with this pack because they keep getting into all the most interesting fights.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Theurge: \u2018Grand Duchess Anastasia Nikolaevna\u2019 (Silver Fang, Homid), busily trying to avert a Second Great War, secure recognition of her royal dignities by the Tribe and make a clean sweep of the various supernatural jack***** claiming to be Rasputin (Who deserved better).<br /> <br /> Currently operating out of Paris, given Russia isn\u2019t likely to extend a warm welcome and she doesn\u2019t actually want to trigger the Second Great War.<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTE: A little research suggests that the historic Anastasia (born 18th June 1901 New Style) was born a few days after a new moon (15th June of that year), so it\u2019s possible she could be the Ragabash if I\u2019ve misunderstood how lunar phases work).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Philodox (Get of Fenris, Lupus): An adopted German who pays rather less attention to mortal politics than they should and who remains fairly confident the Tribe can handle these \u2018National Socialists\u2019 if they get out hand (and/or fail to deliver on all these impressively progressive notions of wildlife preservation)..<br /> <br /> Equally overconfident in their Tribe\u2019s ability to handle the lunatic fringe currently growing into a maniac mullet and outright bonkers sideburns..<br /> <br /> <br /> - Galliard (Bone Gnawer, Homid): Almost certainly a part-time spy for the Soviets, certainly a part-time Communist, actually an Italian. Currently having the time of his life pointing out all the holes in the aggressively-noble thinking of their pack (and singing their lungs out in support of No More Great Wars).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Ahroun (Child of Gaia, ????): Struggling for World Peace since finding inner peace is currently beyond them. <br /> <br /> <br /> Please don\u2019t take this as a final version of the Pack (\u2018New World\u2019 Pack? \u2018Luna\u2019s Glory\u2019 Pack? \u2018Empty Hand\u2019 Pack?): it\u2019s more of an initial sketch inspired by a shared notion.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not certain what the pack totem should be (Though it occurs to me that Zarok might be an interesting pick - if only because Zarok, with his obsessive interest in Honour, provides a complication as much as a blessing* - one assumes that the Eagle\u2019s Nest pack followed Eagle, so having their friendly rivals follow the Planetary Incarna of Jupiter would be symbolically apt).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Given Zarok\u2019s apparent fondness for Silver Fangs and his association with the planet (and presumably the deity) Jupiter, one sometimes wonders if he might have been the Totem of House Conquering Claw: a suitably larger-than-life patron spirit for the Silver Fangs of the Roman Empire, if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T14:34:11-08:00","id":1530204,"title":"","content":"I will mention that all of the Eagle's Nest pack were based on period Pulp archetypes. Vic Stryker was a mix of hard boiled detective and globe trotting adventurer. Dr. Stratus was both aviator and scientist. McNab was the two-fisted brawler and spitfire. Greta Cole the femme fatal and &quot;gentleman&quot; thief. An Lei Sheng the Wu Shu novel hero. I always presumed the others would follow suite with Anastasia being inspired by the stage play (and the animated film inspired by it). The Black Fury likely a Freebooter archeologist, the Bone Gnawer some sort of Mexican &quot;hero of the common people&quot; revolutionary bandit, the Red Talon a Jack London character, the Uktena heavily based in period African American culture, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T15:43:36-08:00","id":1530214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530204#post1530204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will mention that all of the Eagle's Nest pack were based on period Pulp archetypes. Vic Stryker was a mix of hard boiled detective and globe trotting adventurer. Dr. Stratus was both aviator and scientist. McNab was the two-fisted brawler and spitfire. Greta Cole the femme fatal and &quot;gentleman&quot; thief. An Lei Sheng the Wu Shu novel hero. I always presumed the others would follow suite with Anastasia being inspired by the stage play (and the animated film inspired by it). The Black Fury likely a Freebooter archeologist, the Bone Gnawer some sort of Mexican &quot;hero of the common people&quot; revolutionary bandit, the Red Talon a Jack London character, the Uktena heavily based in period African American culture, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're amazing and were pretty much the inspiration for a Pulp Werewolf chronicle I ran once upon a time. Thanks for reminding me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:03:25-08:00","id":1530215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530214#post1530214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, they're amazing and were pretty much the inspiration for a Pulp Werewolf chronicle I ran once upon a time. Thanks for reminding me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tangential: I think that W:tA would do really well with the rules from TC, particularly with Aberrant, if only because Mokole are easier to handle with (nictitating membrane closes over eyes in place of sunglasses) Scale-based mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_NzLs-xSss0\" data-code=\"_NzLs-xSss0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_NzLs-xSss0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T07:35:00-08:00","id":1530272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1530204#post1530204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will mention that all of the Eagle's Nest pack were based on period Pulp archetypes. Vic Stryker was a mix of hard boiled detective and globe trotting adventurer. Dr. Stratus was both aviator and scientist. McNab was the two-fisted brawler and spitfire. Greta Cole the femme fatal and &quot;gentleman&quot; thief. A oven Lei Sheng the Wu Shu novel hero. I always presumed the others would follow suite with Anastasia being inspired by the stage play (and the animated film inspired by it). The Black Fury likely a Freebooter archeologist, the Bone Gnawer some sort of Mexican &quot;hero of the common people&quot; revolutionary bandit, the Red Talon a Jack London character, the Uktena heavily based in period African American culture, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given your avatar, I think it\u2019s easy to see why you have a much keener sense of Pulp than myself! \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> One will certainly give some thought to the take on Anastasia\u2019s pack that you\u2019ve suggested - see if we can puzzle out a more detailed conception of the group between us, though that might be more suitably displayed in another thread (It has occurred to me that this pack could be the \u2018Lion\u2019s Den\u2019 Pack - in the sense that while Vic\u2019s pack are<br /> globetrotting at a furious pace, Anastasia\u2019s pack are more focussed on cleaning up the spiritual carnage and binding up the other wounds left by the Great War (Or at least making sure they aren\u2019t torn open again), which naturally sees them most often operating in places that are very, very dangerous to Garou and over a slightly longer period.<br /> <br /> If the Eagle\u2019s Nest are very Indiana Jones cliffhangers, the \u2018Lion\u2019s Den\u2019 (Lion\u2019s Lip?) pack are more like the murder mystery &amp; spy fiction of the early-to-mid 20th century: another possible analogy - the Eagle\u2019s Nest are playing INDIANA JONES, the Lion\u2019s Lip are playing CALL OF CTHULHU.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a tangentially-related note, it just struck me today that depicting Vic Stryker as an Ace Reporter during his adventuring heyday would help bring out his inner Galliard and also allow him some freedom to dip into everyday society as required (Ach, at this rate I\u2019ll have to set up a HOW I\u2019D RUIN IT thread to get some of my notions for the WEREWOLF setting on record without cluttering up someone else\u2019s thread).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T18:07:55-08:00","id":1530938,"title":"","content":"I tend to like those NPCs in the Rage Books that inspire me to include similar concepts in my own chronicles.<br /> <br /> Grand Prize goes to Bone Juice in Rage Across New York. He's the teenage runaway Bone Gnawer Ahroun who eats other kid runaways by using his milk carton with picture of a missing child fetish to find them. He's a great low level villain. Perfect for the PCs. And a complete distraction to all the important stuff going on in RANY. He really inspired me to make good use of the Maneaters camp of the Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> Second Prize is Guttooth, the Shadow Lord lupus theurge who is the Prophet of Gaia in Dark Alliance. I really like how that sourcebook says it is up to the ST to decide if Guttooth is secretly of the Wyrm, the actual Chosen of Gaia, or something else. Anything that forces players to take a stand and define their characters is a good thing. And because so many players are hesitant to do so UNLESS they know what is the &quot;correct&quot; thing to do, by letting the ST make their own choice a PC cannot metagame it. My favorite Garou NPC I created was for LARP that I made Untrustworthy x3 and told everyone up front OOC that he was. Needless to say I fucked over some people, but not everyone. So the PCs quickly split between people who thought he was just a dick and hated him, to those that thought he was doing good things by whatever means available, to those who thought him misguided or flawed, or those who just wanted to avoid him. But everyone had their own opinion.<br /> <br /> Third Prize is Darius Winchester, Silver Fang king of Australia. Despite coming out before the Silver Fangs tribebook, that sourcebook completely ignores the Winchester family or their kingship of Australia. That alone would probably make me like him. But even better, he's a great mix of good and bad. He's an inbred stutterer already going bald in his thirties. He's also fallen in love (and possibly blood bond) to a Gangrel vampire he met in the woods before she revealed her true nature to him. But he's also a morally principled man who hopes to restore his tribe, his family, and the Garou back to honor by assuaging the anger of the Bunyip, putting their spirits to rest, and atoning for the wrong the Garou did. So I find him an interesting, complex character. An ST can do many things with him, and I imagine the PCs can react in many ways to him depending on how the ST portrays him.<br /> <br /> Runner Up: Ruben Bruckner, the gentle Quaker Pennsylvania Dutch Get of Fenris Ahroun of Rage Across Appalachia. It's a great local concept for a chronicle set in Appalachia. The Quaker Get of Fenris is both totally justified, yet unexpected as a result of too much attention on the game rules instead of real life history. Most games need more of these kinds of concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T03:34:17-08:00","id":1530965,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not going to lie, there\u2019s something insulting-yet-deeply-appropriate about the Silver Fangs of Australia having a King, yet getting no real recognition from the rest of the tribe (One can only wonder if that Vampire Scandal came out of the woodwork between RAGE ACROSS AUSTRALIA and the Tribebook), especially given Australia\u2019s history of Republican agitation.<br /> <br /> On a less insolent note, it\u2019s interesting to note that King Darius Winchester is the second Silver Fang King with a Persian name of whom we are made aware - Cyrus the Bald of House Unbreakable Hearth comes to mind - so it\u2019s interesting to wonder if House Wise Heart got it\u2019s start as Kin to the Persian <i>Shahanshah</i>, in the days of Cyrus the Great.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, \u2018Quaker Get of Fenris\u2019 is a delightfully outr\u00e9 character concept: may I please ask what Auspice they belonged to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T05:18:26-08:00","id":1531466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1529744#post1529744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Favourites, ok.<br /> <br /> Adventure- The Broken Brother<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know this adventure. Was it official/published or your ST's idea? Also does anyone know what happened to W5 Reclamation adventure? Cause I can't find it either on Paradox/Renegade site or Drivethrurpg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T05:50:45-08:00","id":1531467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1531466#post1531466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know this adventure. Was it official/published or your ST's idea? Also does anyone know what happened to W5 Reclamation adventure? Cause I can't find it either on Paradox/Renegade site or Drivethrurpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its for Werewolf: The Savage Age but its fairly easy to convert to Modern Day. You can find it on STV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T08:41:57-08:00","id":1531518,"title":"","content":"Having read up on the Sept of the Western Eye - I recently finished PRINCE OF THE CITY and wanted to reassure my<br /> self that the Bay Area Garou were better led (and just BETTER at what they did) than the Lupine minister depicted in it\u2019s pages (or, for that matter, the clown who picked a fight with a ghoul at a parley AND LOST) - I\u2019ve discovered a nameless Garou who has just become one of my favourite allusions in the whole setting.<br /> <br /> This would be the Wendigo student studying under Morihei High Mountain (A Stargazer resident in the area who also finds time to help a local Nosferatu seeking Golconda).<br /> <br /> If you have to ask why I find the notion of a Native American warrior studying to become a Kung Fu Werewolf DELIGHTFUL then we may have very different tastes in WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE (Amongst other things).<br /> <br /> (Oddly enough, my initial reaction was to wonder if this might be Hollywood Werewolf John \u2018True Arrow\u2019 Blackfeather - or a member of his pack).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T07:07:19-08:00","id":1531619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1531518#post1531518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Having read up on the Sept of the Western Eye - I recently finished PRINCE OF THE CITY and wanted to reassure my<br /> self that the Bay Area Garou were better led (and just BETTER at what they did) than the Lupine minister depicted in it\u2019s pages (or, for that matter, the clown who picked a fight with a ghoul at a parley AND LOST) - I\u2019ve discovered a nameless Garou who has just become one of my favourite allusions in the whole setting.<br /> <br /> This would be the Wendigo student studying under Morihei High Mountain (A Stargazer resident in the area who also finds time to help a local Nosferatu seeking Golconda).<br /> <br /> If you have to ask why I find the notion of a Native American warrior studying to become a Kung Fu Werewolf DELIGHTFUL then we may have very different tastes in WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE (Amongst other things).<br /> <br /> (Oddly enough, my initial reaction was to wonder if this might be Hollywood Werewolf John \u2018True Arrow\u2019 Blackfeather - or a member of his pack).</div> </div> </div> </div>Check if Edmonton Oilers didn't play Los Angeles Kings that time. If yes it could also be Owen Robinson <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T13:10:52-08:00","id":1531795,"title":"","content":"Another thing I love about Werewolf are the Glass Walkers and their bizzaro marriage of technology (in the context of hardware and proceses). You have a tribe that has decided to take up ideas that humans engage with and then build them, remix them, reimagine them and interact with them on a technological, spiritual and practical level. This strange marriage has brought us kinfolk-garou spec ops squads, cybernetically enhanced Garou with spirit awakened shapeshifting technology, Catholic Mobsters, reality hackers, the cutting edge of modern spirits married with modern tech, asian action stars, corporate raiders in literal and symbollic sense...<br /> <br /> This diversity and flair of the Glass Walker tribe echoes the depth and flavour of WtA and how delightfully clever and fun it gets around to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T13:12:18-08:00","id":1531796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1531795#post1531795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I love about Werewolf are the Glass Walkers and their bizzaro marriage of technology (in the context of hardware and proceses). You have a tribe that has decided to take up ideas that humans engage with and then build them, remix them, reimagine them and interact with them on a technological, spiritual and practical level. This strange marriage has brought us kinfolk-garou spec ops squads, cybernetically enhanced Garou with spirit awakened shapeshifting technology, Catholic Mobsters, reality hackers, the cutting edge of modern spirits married with modern tech, asian action stars, corporate raiders in literal and symbollic sense...<br /> <br /> This diversity and flair of the Glass Walker tribe echoes the depth and flavour of WtA and how delightfully clever and fun it gets around to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>City Farmers are a vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:14:55-08:00","id":1531959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1531619#post1531619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check if Edmonton Oilers didn't play Los Angeles Kings that time. If yes it could also be Owen Robinson <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div> Though wouldn\u2019t a career in the NHL already qualify as intense Martial Arts training anyway?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I am now extremely tempted to suggest that John Blackfeather is absolutely a member of The Hounds (Or at least a graduate of the same school), because why not have two celebrity Garou in one pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T13:32:42-08:00","id":1532253,"title":"","content":"Everything.<br /> WtA 2ed was my first serious rpg attempt and I fell in love from the first side of comic book that was translated in my country. From there it's on the top. It's a part of my life, brings the best memories from the best sessions I've run and played. That is why I am so interested in the game state.<br /> I was thrilled by Deadlands x Wild West and played the trilogy and Billy Stormwalker is tough and one of my favourite garou.<br /> The Morningnkill line- Isaiah, tragedy of Jacob rising without father and of course Albrecht - love the lore and novels.<br /> Margrave and Shadow Lords with their camps - amazing stuff , for example Lightbringers. Red Talons with the best revised Tribebook. Book of the Weaver witch is scary- read it and confirm to nowday reality- Technocrats are real and some concepts and plans I've heared about are so similar to ideas from book that it is frightening me lot.<br /> All the tribes have some unique magic and that makes the game Good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T07:07:51-07:00","id":1532767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1531959#post1531959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though wouldn\u2019t a career in the NHL already qualify as intense Martial Arts training anyway?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I am now extremely tempted to suggest that John Blackfeather is absolutely a member of The Hounds (Or at least a graduate of the same school), because why not have two celebrity Garou in one pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not have four? Look at Spooky Tooth, a thrash metal band from GW tribebook. If we talk about furry celebrities there were also Lila Westerly, a Glass Walker supermodel from Malafaxus three part adventure from White Wolf Magazine, Widdershins (either as a folk band or as part of the society; I know they are kinfolk but that still counts) or Anya Z, goth music queen from Bastet breedbook among a few others. Heck, even my PCs once formed a metal band which played before Spooky Tooth on their tour and achieve a minor success <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for mentioned Wendigo student of Morihei I used him once as part of &quot;superheroes&quot; pack during a mental exercise with my friend. He was of part Siberakh part wind spirit (merit from Wendigo tribebook) stock. I know, it's kinda Haights-like overkill but we tried a few times to check how to bend the rules to create overpowered characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 03-17-2024, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T15:14:34-07:00","id":1532782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529718-the-fluffy-puppy-thread-post-your-favorite-npcs-characters-and-things-about-w-ta?p=1532767#post1532767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not have four? Look at Spooky Tooth, a thrash metal band from GW tribebook. If we talk about furry celebrities there were also Lila Westerly, a Glass Walker supermodel from Malafaxus three part adventure from White Wolf Magazine, Widdershins (either as a folk band or as part of the society; I know they are kinfolk but that still counts) or Anya Z, goth music queen from Bastet breedbook among a few others. Heck, even my PCs once formed a metal band which played before Spooky Tooth on their tour and achieve a minor success <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for mentioned Wendigo student of Morihei I used him once as part of &quot;superheroes&quot; pack during a mental exercise with my friend. He was of part Siberakh part wind spirit (merit from Wendigo tribebook) stock. I know, it's kinda Haights-like overkill but we tried a few times to check how to bend the rules to create overpowered characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it vaguely hilarious that the real life Spooky Tooth, in its oughties incarnation, had a guitarist named Joey Albrecht.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T04:51:24-07:00","id":1532805,"title":"","content":"For some strange reason, whenever I type the name SPOOKY TOOTH it always appears in Full Caps - but then The \u2018Tooth is Larger than Life by definition, being \u2018SPINAL TAP with Werewolves!\u2019 (Can we agree that if you want to smuggle in some of the more delightfully OTT names from WEREWOLF products into the actual World of Darkness then SPOOKY TOOTH is the way to do it? Tell me they never mounted a WORLD OF RAGE tour, complete with merchandise, and I must tell you that you LIE!).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not going to lie, it\u2019s very easy to imagine a \u2018documentary\u2019 discussing how Insanely Awesome and Awesomely Insane the \u2018Tooth were, back in their brief moment of Glory (\u201cWhen the \u2018Tooth bought the house down, you walked away through the rubble, man!\u201d): I\u2019d suspect that modern Garou elders are torn between \u201cBut the VEIL\u201d and \u201cThose were the days!\u201d.